  "summary": "Red, black and gold berry-vine painting on wooden tableware, gold without a grain of real gold.",
  "description": "Khokhloma turns cheap wooden spoons, bowls and khokhloma-style cups into \"gold\" tableware: vessels primed with clay, coated with drying oil and tin powder, painted with rowan berries, strawberry vines and firebirds in red, black and green, then lacquered and oven-fired until the tin glows like gilding. Old Believer settlers and monastery craftsmen shaped the tradition in the Volga forests; mass Soviet production spread it worldwide as the emblem of Russian folk design. The palette is strictly disciplined — gold ground, scarlet and black ornament.",
